            <ArticleTitle>Counting copy number and calories.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>852-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/ng.3365</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Copy number variation (CNV) at several genomic loci has been associated with different human traits and diseases, but in many cases the findings could not be replicated. A new study provides insights into the degree of variation present at the amylase locus and calls into question a previous association between amylase copy number and body mass index.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
